From: Bjorn Helgaas <bhelgaas@google.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:04:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Expose devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release()
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.3.6
Git-commit: 39d1c645bb99d8bd7e6f5b0183b192f30c88d917

[ Upstream commit 39d1c645bb99d8bd7e6f5b0183b192f30c88d917 ]

devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge() allocates a struct pci_host_bridge and also
parses device tree resources and claims them.  There are drivers, e.g.,
pcie-iproc-bcma.c, that need to allocate a pci_host_bridge but do not need
device tree resources.

Expose devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release() so they can avoid the device
tree parts by calling pci_alloc_host_bridge() directly and adding the devm
release function manually.

[bhelgaas: add EXPORT_SYMBOL]
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Helgaas <bhelgaas@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261013220421.1588051-2-bhelgaas@google.com
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/pci/pci.h   | 1 +
 drivers/pci/probe.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci.h b/drivers/pci/pci.h
index 5b3dd1adbf35..0ede46012339 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci.h
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.h
@@ -502,6 +502,7 @@ enum pci_bar_type {
 	pci_bar_mem64,		/* A 64-bit memory BAR */
 };
 
+void devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release(void *data);
 struct device *pci_get_host_bridge_device(struct pci_dev *dev);
 void pci_put_host_bridge_device(struct device *dev);
 
diff --git a/drivers/pci/probe.c b/drivers/pci/probe.c
index 7738ebffb609..46121c22b26b 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/probe.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/probe.c
@@ -696,10 +696,11 @@ struct pci_host_bridge *pci_alloc_host_bridge(size_t priv)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(pci_alloc_host_bridge);
 
-static void devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release(void *data)
+void devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release(void *data)
 {
 	pci_free_host_bridge(data);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge_release);
 
 struct pci_host_bridge *devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge(struct device *dev,
 						   size_t priv)
-- 
